{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A gate name or command containing a credential can place that credential unredacted in a persisted verification artifact."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"On resume, a script map with both \"ok\" and \"output\" is corrupted and persisted, causing false blocking audit findings."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resumed shadow-review error containing a credential is copied unredacted into a stored artifact."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Restored evidence containing terminal escapes can alter the presentation of owner diagnostics when printed."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A citation copied from a redacted requirement can produce misleading validation feedback, although the verification verdict is unchanged."}]}